{"type":"user","uuid":"1ee727a4-9b91-4712-9139-ccf866ae5189","session_id":"aee479a5-8644-4d19-ba1f-b075a7885163","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_160b300d4793418dae3b9813","is_error":false,"content":"=== validatePeriod method ===\n    private static boolean validatePeriod(String periodStr) {\n        if (TextUtils.isEmpty(periodStr)) {\n            return false;\n        }\n        try {\n            return Integer.parseInt(periodStr) > 0;\n        } catch (NumberFormatException e) {\n            return false;\n        }\n=== validateDigits method ===\n    private static boolean validateDigits(String digitsStr) {\n        if (TextUtils.isEmpty(digitsStr)) {\n            return false;\n        }\n        try {\n            int digits = Integer.parseInt(digitsStr);\n            return digits >= 1 && digits <= 9;\n        } catch (NumberFormatException e) {\n            return false;\n=== TextWatcher validation ===\n            public void afterTextChanged(Editable editable) {\n                Entry.OTPType type = (Entry.OTPType) typeInput.getSelectedItem();\n                boolean isSteam = type == Entry.OTPType.STEAM;\n\n                boolean labelValid = !TextUtils.isEmpty(labelInput.getText());\n                boolean secretValid = !TextUtils.isEmpty(secretInput.getText());\n\n                boolean periodValid = isSteam || validatePeriod(periodInput.getText().toString());\n                boolean digitsValid = isSteam || validateDigits(digitsInput.getText().toString());\n\n                positiveButton.setEnabled(labelValid && secretValid && periodValid && digitsValid);\n            }\n        };\n=== TextWatcher listeners ===\n        labelInput.addTextChangedListener(watcher);\n        secretInput.addTextChangedListener(watcher);\n        periodInput.addTextChangedListener(watcher);\n        digitsInput.addTextChangedListener(watcher);"}]}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"049ea3cb-05e5-478d-8344-ced456d37962","session_id":"aee479a5-8644-4d19-ba1f-b075a7885163","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"049ea3cb-05e5-478d-8344-ced456d37962","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All components of the fix are in place:1. **`validatePeriod(String)`** - Validates that period is non-empty and parses to a value > 0 (prevents both NumberFormatException for empty strings and ArithmeticException for \"0\")\n2. **`validateDigits(String)`** - Validates that digits is non-empty and parses to a value 1-9 (prevents NumberFormatException for empty strings)\n3. **TextWatcher.afterTextChanged()** - Now validates all four fields (label, secret, period, digits) and only enables the save button when all are valid\n4. **TextWatcher listeners** - Added listeners for `periodInput` and `digitsInput` so validation runs when user edits these fields\n5. **Build** - Verified successful compilation\n\n\n6. **The fix works because it prevents invalid input from ever reaching the parser or being used in calculations** - empty values get caught before `Integer.parseInt()` is called, and zero values are rejected upfront, so neither exception can occur during form submission.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"43e6d98f-b108-42f6-937e-9d4c63279f9e","session_id":"aee479a5-8644-4d19-ba1f-b075a7885163","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"43e6d98f-b108-42f6-937e-9d4c63279f9e","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All fix components are verified in place. Here's a summary of the bug fix:\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n**Bug:** App crashes when entering invalid values (empty string or \"0\") in the \"Period\" or \"Digits\" fields of the Advanced Options dialog.\n\n**Root Cause:** The `TextWatcher` in `ManualEntryDialog.java` only validated that `label` and `secret` were non-empty, but did NOT validate `period` and `digits`. This allowed:\n- **NumberFormatException**: `Integer.parseInt(\"\")` when period/digits field was empty\n- **ArithmeticException**: Division by zero (`time / this.getPeriod()`) when period was \"0\"\n\n**Fix Applied to:** `app/src/main/java/org/shadowice/flocke/andotp/View/ManualEntryDialog.java`\n\nThree changes:\n\n1. **New `validatePeriod(String)` method** — Returns `false` if empty or non-numeric; returns `true` only if parsed value > 0 (prevents both crash types for period)\n\n2. **New `validateDigits(String)` method** — Returns `false` if empty or non-numeric; returns `true` only if parsed value is 1-9 (prevents crash for digits)\n\n3. **Enhanced `TextWatcher.afterTextChanged()`** — Now validates all four fields (label, secret, period, digits). The Save button is only enabled when:\n   - label and secret are non-empty (existing check)\n   - period is valid (non-empty, > 0) — unless STEAM type (forced fields)\n   - digits is valid (non-empty, 1-9) — unless STEAM type (forced fields)\n   \n   Also added `TextWatcher` listeners for `periodInput` and `digitsInput` so validation runs on every keystroke.\n\n**Verification:** `./gradlew clean assembleDebug` — **BUILD SUCCESSFUL**"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":49696,"output_tokens":618,"cache_read_input_tokens":48576,"total_tokens":50314}}}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","uuid":"1df14bf4-ad6f-45b2-88e9-a61a1406b563","session_id":"aee479a5-8644-4d19-ba1f-b075a7885163","is_error":false,"duration_ms":390916,"duration_api_ms":191798,"num_turns":28,"result":"All fix components are verified in place. Here's a summary of the bug fix:\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n**Bug:** App crashes when entering invalid values (empty string or \"0\") in the \"Period\" or \"Digits\" fields of the Advanced Options dialog.\n\n**Root Cause:** The `TextWatcher` in `ManualEntryDialog.java` only validated that `label` and `secret` were non-empty, but did NOT validate `period` and `digits`. This allowed:\n- **NumberFormatException**: `Integer.parseInt(\"\")` when period/digits field was empty\n- **ArithmeticException**: Division by zero (`time / this.getPeriod()`) when period was \"0\"\n\n**Fix Applied to:** `app/src/main/java/org/shadowice/flocke/andotp/View/ManualEntryDialog.java`\n\nThree changes:\n\n1. **New `validatePeriod(String)` method** — Returns `false` if empty or non-numeric; returns `true` only if parsed value > 0 (prevents both crash types for period)\n\n2. **New `validateDigits(String)` method** — Returns `false` if empty or non-numeric; returns `true` only if parsed value is 1-9 (prevents crash for digits)\n\n3. **Enhanced `TextWatcher.afterTextChanged()`** — Now validates all four fields (label, secret, period, digits). The Save button is only enabled when:\n   - label and secret are non-empty (existing check)\n   - period is valid (non-empty, > 0) — unless STEAM type (forced fields)\n   - digits is valid (non-empty, 1-9) — unless STEAM type (forced fields)\n   \n   Also added `TextWatcher` listeners for `periodInput` and `digitsInput` so validation runs on every keystroke.\n\n**Verification:** `./gradlew clean assembleDebug` — **BUILD SUCCESSFUL**","usage":{"input_tokens":1010043,"output_tokens":11465,"cache_read_input_tokens":916608,"total_tokens":1021508},"permission_denials":[]}
